# Local `supabase functions serve` environment.
#
# Copy to supabase/functions/.env — that file is gitignored and never deployed.
#
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN is a comma-separated allowlist. Set it to YOUR dev origin
# so the browser will accept the orchestrator's responses; without it the
# functions fail closed to https://agent.phc-sa.com and every local call is
# blocked before it leaves the tab. That blocking is what hid a real, permanent
# ai-orchestrator failure behind "AI commentary unavailable" until it reached
# production.
#
# Ports come from this repository's own config:
#   .claude/launch.json   → vite dev --port 5173
#   playwright.config.ts  → PLAYWRIGHT_PORT default 8080
#
# Never set this to "*" — these functions read an Authorization header.
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173,http://localhost:8080

# Serve the functions, then point the app at them:
#   supabase functions serve ai-orchestrator --env-file supabase/functions/.env
